               <value>
                  <exData contentType="text/html">
                     <body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/"><p style="text-align:center;font-weight:bold;text-decoration:underline;letter-spacing:0in">UPS 330.164: Posthumous Degree and Recognition</p><p style="text-align:center;font-weight:bold;text-decoration:underline;letter-spacing:0in"><br/></p><p style="letter-spacing:0in">Students who, at the time of their death or prior to an illness or accident that leads to their death, were in good academic standing in a degree program may be awarded a posthumous degree by the President.</p><p style="letter-spacing:0in"><br/></p><p style="letter-spacing:0in">The purpose of the posthumous degree is a recognition of the academic achievement of the student, as well as a statement of their value to the California State University, Fullerton community.</p><p style="letter-spacing:0in"><br/></p><p style="letter-spacing:0in">When determining whether to grant a degree under this policy, the President will consider recommendations from the Chair, Coordinator, or Director of the program for which the degree is being conferred.</p></body>
